      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O'Gara are delighted to present this distinguished four-bedroom semi-detached Victorian residence to the market. Occupying a prime position on the ever-popular Kenilworth Square South, the property is further enhanced by an exceptional south-facing rear garden extending to approximately 105ft, offering rear vehicular access and exciting potential for off-street parking and/or a mews development (sub to pp)\r\n\r\nRequiring refurbishment throughout, No. 66 represents a rare opportunity to acquire a home of immense character and create a truly exceptional family residence in one of Dublin's most sought-after locations. Rich in period detail, the property retains an abundance of original features including impressive ceiling heights, ornate coving, original fireplaces, sash windows and elegant proportions throughout. The generously scaled accommodation reflects the grandeur and craftsmanship synonymous with the Victorian era.\r\n\r\nWhile in need of modernisation, the house provides the perfect blank canvas for a discerning purchaser to restore and reimagine according to their own tastes and requirements. With its superb proportions, original character and outstanding potential, this is a unique opportunity to create a landmark family home of considerable distinction.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises entrance hall, living room, dining room, tv room, kitchen/breakfastroom, downstairs wc. Return: Double bedroom and bathroom. First floor : 2 bedrooms plus nursery/home office.\r\n\r\nKenilworth Square is one of Dublin's most distinguished Victorian squares, developed between 1858 and 1879 during the city's southward expansion. Characterised by its elegant red-brick residences, generous proportions and mature setting, the square has long been regarded as one of the premier residential addresses in Dublin 6. It offers a unique blend of architectural heritage, community spirit and exceptional convenience, all within easy reach of Rathgar Village, Rathmines and Dublin City Centre."
      },
